New object literal created every render → new reference → child sees "changed" prop → re-render.

```jsx
// Bad: new ref each render
<Child config={{ theme: 'dark', size: 14 }} />

// Fix 1: useMemo
const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: 'dark', size: 14 }), []);
<Child config={config} />

// Fix 2: move outside component (if static)
const CONFIG = { theme: 'dark', size: 14 };
function Parent() { return <Child config={CONFIG} />; }

// Fix 3: memo on child (last resort)
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => { ... });
```

JS compare objects by ref, not value. `{} === {}` → false. Same content, different ref = React thinks prop changed.

Pick fix 1 if config depends on state/props. Fix 2 if truly static. Fix 3 if can't control parent.
